  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> For ideals gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pV</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>nRT</mi></math></p><p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>pV</mi><mi>nR</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo></math> constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>083</mn><mo>=</mo></math> constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>PV</mi></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;</p><p>The gas that shows highest product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, has highest temperature.</p><p>for<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atmL</mi></math></p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atmL</mi><mo>&#8201;</mo></math></p><p>(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p>Hence gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> show highest temperature.</p>"
